# Portfolio rules

- One project per numbered folder; do not invent a monorepo framework unless asked.
- Prefer C++20, clear APIs, and tests over clever lock-free code unless the task is explicitly about lock-free design.
- Public headers live under `include/`; keep READMEs short and decision-focused.
- After implementation changes, run the project’s CMake configure/build/`ctest` loop from `AGENTS.md`.
- Do not change public APIs without explicit user approval.
- IntelliSense: new `NN-*` projects are picked up by `scripts/generate_compile_commands.py` (via `cmake/PortfolioIde.cmake`). If the new project depends on another folder, add it to `IDE_DEPS` in that script. Do not hand-edit per-test include hacks.
